{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01PWE9wjAJQBTfSKDtzKgBGa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (plain markdown files as source of truth, Python stdlib only).\n\n- **Purpose** â€” It's a calm, local \"second brain\" + task manager: tracks tasks, projects, an inbox, and per-domain work (academic, commercial, family, writing) across a task lifecycle (active â†’ done / cancelled / saved-for-later â†’ restored).\n\n- **Core app** â€” `anchor_gui.py` is a self-contained Python HTTP server (stdlib only) that renders an interactive browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777`, writing changes straight back to the markdown files. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` (you don't launch it by hand). `anchor.py` is a CLI mirror of the same logic that also generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **R&D \"trio\" control surface** â€” Beyond plain task management, it has grown a mission-control layer for managing AI-assisted R&D projects driven by a three-skill \"trio\" (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman). Built across four versions (v2 sessions/summaries/grass, v3 \"Mission Control,\" v4 \"Project Cockpit\" â€” all merged to master). Each project window is a single-screen cockpit where each lane (Research/Planning/Build/Deliverables/Grass) is a tile with one honest status light; clicking expands an inline panel with a cached summary on top and a real resizable terminal below.\n\n- **What it ships under that surface** â€” real **ConPTY terminals** (xterm.js over a hand-rolled WebSocket / SSE), per-session **git-worktree isolation**, a durable session registry, an **engine toggle** (Claude â†” Gemini), proactive **cached/validated summaries**, cost/tokens/time **rollups**, stage **handoffs**, type-aware **deliverable launch** (skill/tool/service/program/doc), and a runnable deliverable **preview server** (always on a free port, hard-guarded â‰  8777). Branded as a Ghost World Labs tool.\n\n- **What it ships operationally** â€” a daily 5 AM **health-check** (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) that fully stub-walks the v2/v3/v4 surfaces without touching live data, writing reports to `health_reports/`; plus desktop launchers, a single-instance bind guard (`SO_EXCLUSIVEADDRUSE`), and a deny-by-default distribution builder (`distro.py`) that enforces the stdlib-only rule with one declared exception: the optional `pywinpty` terminal extra.\n\n- **One declared dependency exception** â€” everything is Python stdlib except the v3+ terminal subsystem's optional `pywinpty` (`import winpty`, lazy, in `pty_manager.py` only; `pip install .[terminal]`), which degrades gracefully if absent.\n\nThe current branch (`foreman/rnd-v4.1-cockpit`) has uncommitted work-in-progress on a v4.1 cockpit iteration (rendering the project window as the real Paradigm-2 layout)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4310,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24814,"cache_read_input_tokens":20597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24814},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17ca130a-0aa4-46f9-bf02-66610b644716","uuid":"33b9db80-086f-436b-b7eb-dff9382b4048","request_id":"req_011Cc2GrdNbTudCkw2JTBtbt"}
